EXTENSION "ArM5_Faith_and_Flame_Arelat_AlazaisOfMercereChiefRedcapAndFirstConsulOfTheCoenobium" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, Faith & Flame - Alazais of Mercere, Chief Redcap and First Consul of the Coenobium"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ArM5_Faith_and_Flame_Core_Ext"

    # Alazais of Mercere, Chief Redcap and First Consul of the Coenobium (Chapter Eight: Arelat, p131): one character, its printed stat lines verbatim fields, its write-up the DESCRIPTION.

    #t49aa0458e0ff4d3415d60a ^"Alazais of Mercere, Chief Redcap and First Consul of the Coenobium" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Magus"
            ^"Covenant" LIST [#t6db295248a1e5be20cb0ac ^"Coenobium Rhodanien"]
            ^"Age" STRING "59 (Apparent Age: 27)"
            ^"Personality Traits" STRING "Ambitious +6, Wily +3, Patient +2"
            ^"Source" STRING "Faith & Flame"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 131
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Claiming descent from Helen of Troy, the First Consul and Chief Redcap wears a tragic mask once favored by classical actors. She never removes her mask except in the presence of magi or her lover, an unGifted folk witch ally of the Coenobium for whom she has obtained a long-lasting Longevity Ritual at great cost with help from the Praeco, Dama. Rumor has it that she was once attacked with alchemical acid by a former suitor, leaving her face hideously scarred but none of the other magi will either confirm or deny this.\n\nUnGifted, she nevertheless makes much of a claim to be directly descended from the Founder Mercere though his grandaughter, using it to engender respect amongst Redcaps and the Jerbiton magi alike. Alazais’s leadership has seen an increasing number of non-Jerbiton magi being accepted as semipermanent or permanent guests and the adoption of a number of lesser hedge wizards as nominal Redcaps.\n\nAlthough careful to maintain the appearance of never voting openly in council meetings, she quietly pulls the strings behind the scenes, maneuvering the might of the Coenobium to further her own goals. She is careful to maintain the guise of encouraging the Jerbiton magi to seek beauty and leave the mundane tasks of running the covenant to their supposed inferiors."
    }

}
